## VERDICT: SOUND-WITH-CAPS

The model is an **excellent ranker and a safe accept/reject gate**, but its **P values are
not trustworthy as probabilities in the 0.2ג€“0.8 "maybe" range**, and its **singleton band is
under-validated and optimistic**. Deploy the run as-is for tier-A (P never touches tier A) and
for coarse tier-B accept/reject; apply the caps below in the **deck builder** before any human
review, and correct the "isotonic per length" framing (see ֲ§3).

**Integrity check passed:** my independent re-implementation of `p_deploy` reproduces the
model's stored `reliability_margin` table **bucket-for-bucket** (0.0ג€“0.1 ג†’ 0.002 on n=92,088;
0.9ג€“1.0 ג†’ 0.981 on n=1,151; every intermediate bucket matches). All numbers below are therefore
faithful to the deployed lookup.

### The 5 numbers that matter
1. **AUC = 0.9909** overall (12,746 pos / 839,990 neg); **0.958** within hard cases (alen<80).
   Ranking is strong; the problem is calibration, not separation.
2. **Extremes are well-calibrated:** P<0.1 bucket ג†’ **0.2%** empirical (834,921 rows);
   Pג‰¥0.9 bucket ג†’ **98.5%** empirical (9,961 rows). These two buckets hold ~99% of all mass.
3. **Mid-range is badly miscalibrated:** the small-margin bands miss by **+0.18 to +0.70**
   (e.g. `m_0_003`/alen-100 predicts 0.31, empirical 0.80; `m_0_003`/alen-200 predicts 0.11,
   empirical 0.81) and **גˆ’0.27 to גˆ’0.41** the other way (`m_0_003`/alen-60 predicts 0.49,
   empirical 0.08). Non-monotone in length.
4. **The length feature has collapsed:** aligned length `alen` clusters at **median ~66 for
   EVERY crop length** (len-40 crops ג†’ alen mean 69.6; len-300 crops ג†’ alen mean 77.7). The
   model fits 7 length curves but deploys ~2 (alen-60 receives 68% of rows, alen-80 22%); the
   len-40 curve is selected for **0.5%** of len-40 rows.
5. **Singleton band = 11 labeled rows total.** Decoy null gives Pג‰¥0.90 for singletons out to
   density ~0.45ג€“0.50 at every length, yet **chance matches themselves reach density ~0.50**
   (decoy p05=0.50 at alen-40). Unvalidated and optimistic in the 0.3ג€“0.55 density range.

---

## Findings ranked by severity

| # | Severity | Finding |
|---|----------|---------|
| 1 | **HIGH** | Mid-range P (0.2ג€“0.8) is miscalibrated by up to ֲ±0.4ג€“0.7 in the small-margin bands (`m_003_010`, `m_0_003`) ג€” the discovery-relevant "maybe" zone. Treat P as an **ordinal grade**, not a probability, in this range. |
| 2 | **HIGH** | Length-feature collapse: `alen` ג‰ˆ 66 regardless of crop length; isotonic is **fit by crop-len** but **deployed/validated by alen** ג†’ within-bin population shift and 2ג€“3 curves doing all the work. Root cause of #1. **Re-fit isotonic by alen bin.** |
| 3 | **HIGH** | Singleton band under-validated (11 labeled rows) and optimistic (Pג‰¥0.9 to density ~0.45); decoy null is contaminated by identity shuffles at short alen (CHUNK=25 on a 40-char crop is 50% identity). **Cap it.** |
| 4 | **MED-HIGH** | `RARITY_MAX=60` still hardcoded in `build_smoke_preview2.py` (pilot BLOCKER, not yet fixed). Must become a quantile of the full-corpus tier-A witness distribution ג€” ֲ§6 gives the exact procedure. |
| 5 | **MED** | Competitor/margin definition **differs** between calibration (all candidate works of a single-span crop) and deployment (span-overlap ג‰¥ 0.5 only). Identical on single-span crops, **divergent and untested on multi-work pages** ג€” where the margin band is decided. |
| 6 | **MED** | Small-margin bands have tiny *effective* (per-work-weighted) n; `MARGIN_FIT_FLOOR=20` counts raw rows only. Isotonic overfits ג†’ the non-monotone-in-length curves in #1. |
| 7 | **PASS** | Bucketing-parity BLOCKER (Codex #2) **fix held**: `p_deploy` and `PModel.p` are logically identical and both key on `alen`; holdout reliability is computed through `p_deploy`, so validation and deployment use the same bin. Verified line-by-line (ֲ§5). |
| 8 | **LOW** | Pooled per-length model is effectively dead code at deploy (all 4 non-singleton bands fitted for all 7 lengths ג†’ fallback never taken). Harmless. `not_best`/alen-300 mildly under-predicts (0.012 vs 0.083 empirical) ג€” safe direction. |

